hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3796","Muhammad ibn Mansour al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, and we asked him “about a man who came for Umrah.” So he circumambulated the Kaaba and did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah. Did he come to its family? He said to us: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and circumambulated the Kaaba. Seven times, he prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and circumambulated between Safa and Marwah, and there was for you a good example in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3797","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who joined the prayers, performed one circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3798","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, “Indeed, Ibn Umar established Hajj and Umrah, and he circumambulated One, and he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3799","Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqi told me, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani, Ayoub bin Musa, and Ismail bin Umayyah. And Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, said: “Abdullah ibn Umar went out, and when he came to Dhu al-Hulayfah, he was permitted to perform Umrah. He walked a little and was afraid that He was turned away from the Kaaba, and he said: If I am prevented, I will do as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. He said: By God, the path of Hajj is only the path of Umrah. I bear witness to you that I have made obligatory Hajj with my Umrah, so he walked until he came a short time ago and bought a gift with it, then he came to Mecca and circumambulated the Kaaba seven times, and between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and he said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do.”"
"3800","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah is Ibn Umar, and Abdul Aziz means Ibn Abi Rawwad. They narrate on the authority of Nafi’, who said: “Ibn Umar went out intending to perform Hajj at a time when Al-Hajjaj stayed with Ibn al-Zubayr, and he was told: If there was a fight between them, we feared that They repel you, so he said: Indeed, there is a good example for you in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I will do as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did. I bear you as witness. I have made it obligatory for Umrah to the point that when he was in Dhahr al-Bayda, he said: Hajj and Umrah are only one thing. I bear witness that I have made it obligatory He performed Hajj with Umrah and presented a gift that he had recently bought, so he set off and came to Mecca, circumambulating the Kaaba and Safa and Marwah. He did not do more than that. He slaughtered, but did not shave, nor did he cut his hair, nor did he permit himself of any of the things of which he had been deprived, until the day of the sacrifice came, and he slaughtered and shaved, and saw that he had completed the sacrifice. His first circumambulation for Hajj and Umrah, he said: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did."
"3801","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Musa bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The black stone is from Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3802","Imran bin Musa Al-Basri informed us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “I did not neglect to receive The Stone has been in ease and without difficulty since I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, receiving it.”"
"3803","Saeed bin Yaqoub Al-Talqani reported, saying: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, who said: “Umar approached the stone. So he kissed him and said: I know that you are a stone that does no harm or benefit, and had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kiss you, I would not have kissed you."
"3804","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus and Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Salem, that his father told him, saying: “Umar kissed the stone, then said: By God, I knew that you were a stone, and had I not seen the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he will kiss you as I have kissed you.” Amr said: Zayd bin Aslam told me something similar, on the authority of his father."
"3805","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus and Jarir reported, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abis bin Rabi’ah, he said: “I saw Omar He came to Al-Hijr and said: I know that you are a stone, and had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kissing you, I would not have kissed you. Then he approached From him, so he kissed him.”"
"3806","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, saying: Wakee’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghaflah, “Umar kissed the stone and pressed against it, and said: I saw Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, warmly greeting you.”"
"3807","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar al-Humsi reported, saying: Al-Walid told us, he is Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Hanzalah, he is Ibn Abi Sufyan said: I saw Tawus, who is Ibn Kaysan, passing through the corner. If he found any crowding, he would pass by without crowding, and if he saw it empty, he would kiss it three times. Then he said: I saw Ibn Abbas doing the same, then Ibn Abbas said: I saw Omar Ibn Al-Khattab doing the same, then he said: You A stone that neither benefits nor harms. Had I not seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, kiss you, I would not have kissed you. Then Omar said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, did something like that.”"
"3808","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar al-Homsi told me, saying: Shuaib, who is Ibn Ishaq, told us on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “In the Farewell Pilgrimage, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went around the Kaaba on a camel to receive the pillar.” Because of his dislike for people to turn away from him.”"
"3809","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala and Sulayman bin Dawud Abu Al-Rabi’ reported on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated on a camel during the Farewell Pilgrimage.” He receives the corner with a mahjin.”"
"3810","Othman bin Abdullah bin Kharzad told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Arara told me, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid bin Jabr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to receive the pillar.” With his eyelid, and he kisses the eyelid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3811","Bishr bin Hilal Al-Sawwaf Masri reported, saying: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Mahran, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to circumambulate the House on his mount, and when he reached a corner, he pointed to it.”"
"3812","Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi reported on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id, saying: Yahya, who is al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi`, he said Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: “I have not neglected receiving these two pillars since I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, receiving them.” “The Yemeni and the Hijr are in distress and there is no comfort.”"
"3813","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He receives the Yemeni Corner and the Hijr from every circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3814","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he wiped away the entirety of the House, except for the two Yemeni corners.”"
"3815","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, “Indeed, a man said: O Abu Abd The Most Gracious, I do not see you touching except these two pillars. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Indeed, wiping them is humiliating. \sin\"""""
"3816","Muhammad ibn al-Ala reported to Abu Kurayb al-Kufi, saying: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, Ibn Jurayj, and Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Ubaid bin Jurayj, said: “I said to Ibn Umar: I saw that you did not recognize any of the pillars except these two! He said: I did not see the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, except for these two pillars.” Brief (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3817","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not touch anything except the Yemeni Stone and the Yemeni Corner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3818","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading from him, while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Yunus told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not greet any of the corners of the house except the corner.” Al-Aswad and the one next to it, towards the turn of Al-Jumahayin.”"
"3819","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid Makki, on the authority of his father On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying between the Yemeni corner and the stone: “Our Lord, give us in this world.” good, and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the torment of the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3820","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Yaqoub bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the first circumambulation of Hajj and Umrah, he would make three circumambulations and walk four. Another prays two prostrations, then circumambulates between Safa and Marwah.”"
"3821","Abdul-A'la bin Wasil bin Abdul-A'la told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja'far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father On the authority of Jabir, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Mecca, he entered the mosque and received the stone, then proceeded to his right, and laid three stones on his hands. He walked for four, then he came to the Maqam, and said: And take the place of Abraham as a place of prayer, and he prayed two rak’ahs, and the Maqam is between him and the House. Then he came House after the two rak'ahs, then he received the stone, then went out to Al-Safa.\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3822","Muhammad and Abd al-Rahman, the sons of Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam, informed me on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of his father al-Layth, on the authority of Kathir ibn Farqad, On the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar, “He used to tramp during his tawaf when he came from Hajj or Umrah three days, and then walk four times. He said: And he was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3823","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id Abu Qudamah reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, “Indeed, Abdullah was “The three would throw sand and the four would walk, and he would claim that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"3824","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh and Suleiman bin Dawud Abu Al-Rabi’ reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he came to Mecca, touching the Black Corner first. He goes around, goes around, three times out of the seven.”"
"3825","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sand made of black stone until three circumambulations reached it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3826","Qutayba bin Saeed and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only strove between Safa and al-Marwah and the House to show the polytheists his strength.” The wording is by Abd By God, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He only tried. I did not understand him as I wanted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3827","Muhammad bin Sulayman Luwayn al-Masisi informed me, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “When he presented The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The polytheists said: The fever of Yathrib weakened them, and they encountered evil from it. So God made His Prophet aware of that, and he commanded He told his companions to spread sand, and to walk between the two corners, and the polytheists were in the area of Al-Hijr, so they said: These people have more lashes than such-and-such.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3828","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, “She came to Mecca while she was sick, so she mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Go around behind the worshipers while you Riding, she said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was at the Kaaba reciting “The Surah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3829","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: He informed me Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of a man who recognized the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The circumambulation is a prayer, so when you circumambulate, speak little.” The wording is from Joseph. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3830","Qutayba bin Saeed narrated, he said: Abu Awanah narrated, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Circumambulation of the Kaaba” Prayer, so speak less of it.”"
"3831","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, he said: Sufyan reported, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr reported, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this house and praying at any hour he wants.” \Night or day\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3832","Muhammad ibn Bashar reported, he said: Muhammad reported, he said: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Salamah, he is Ibn Kuhail, he said: I heard Muslim al-Bateen, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The woman used to circumambulate the Kaaba while she was naked and say: Today some or all of it has appeared, but it did not appear.” So I do not permit it. He said: Then it was revealed: “O children of Adam, take your adornment at every mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3833","Abu Dawud Sulaiman bin Saif Al-Harrani reported, saying: Ya’qub told us, he is the son of Abraham, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, That Humaid bin Abdul Rahman informed him: That Abu Hurairah informed him: “That Abu Bakr sent him on the Hajj he had commanded him to carry out.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, before the Farewell Pilgrimage in a group, would call out to the people: Should a polytheist not perform Hajj after the year, and let him not circumambulate the House? \naked\"""""
"3834","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told me, meaning Ghandar, and Uthman bin Omar, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Muharrar bin Abi Hurairah, on the authority of his father, said: “I was with Ali bin Abi Talib when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent him to the people of Mecca with innocence. He said: What were you calling for? He said: We were calling out that only a believing soul will enter Paradise, and no naked person will go around the House. And whoever has a covenant between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, postpone it or extend it to four months, then when the four months have passed The months, for God is free from the polytheists and His Messenger, and no polytheist will perform Hajj after the year. So I was calling until my voice became clear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3835","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Muharrar ibn Abi Hurairah, he said: he said Abu Hurairah: “I was calling out with Ali when he called out the call to prayer for the polytheists. We used to say, ‘No polytheist will perform Hajj after our year, nor will anyone circumambulate the Kaaba naked, nor Only a believer will enter Paradise, and whoever has a period of time between him and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then his term is four months. When four months have passed, God and His Messenger are free from the polytheists.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3836","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ata’, who is Ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, “that a man He said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, I do not see you praying except these two pillars. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Indeed. Anointing them removes sin, and I heard him say: Whoever circumambulates seven days, it is as free as a slave.”"
"3837","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: “I asked Ibn Omar about Mu’tamir, and he came and gave He went to the House and did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah. Should he come to its family? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and circumambulated the House seven days and prayed. He performed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam and circumambulated seven times between Safa and Marwah, and there was for you a good example in the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3838","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi reported, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Kathir bin Kathir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abi Meekness, he said: “I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when he had finished the seven tawafs, he came and prayed two rak’ahs, and there was no one between him and the two tawafs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3839","Amr bin Othman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar al-Homsi reported, on the authority of al-Walid, who is the son of Muslim al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ja`far Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and reached the place of Abraham, he recited: And they took From the place of Abraham, he prayed, and he prayed two rak'ahs, and he recited the Fatiha of the Book, and say, O disbelievers, and say, He is God, the One, then he returned to Corner, so he received it and then went out to Al-Safa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3840","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail is the son of Ja’far reported, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated seven times, prayed three times and walked four times, then he recited, and they took the place of Abraham as a place of prayer, so he prayed. He prostrated two times. He made the place between himself and the Kaaba, then he touched the corner, then he left and said: Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God. We begin. Because of what God began with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3841","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dallawayh reported, saying: Hushaym told us, he said: Asim and Mughirah reported, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Hushaym told us, He said: Asim told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drank from Zamzam while standing.”"
"3842","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I gave the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he drank while standing."
"3843","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: “When the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Mecca. He circumambulated the House seven times, then prayed two rak’ahs behind the shrine, then went out to Safa through the door through which he exits. So he circumambulated Safa and Marwah. Shu’bah said: Ayoub told me, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: Sunnah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3844","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, he said: Asim Al-Ahwal told me, he said: “I said to Anas bin Malik: Did you dislike tawaf between Safa and Marwah until the verse was revealed? He said: Yes, we disliked tawaf between them because they are rituals. Pre-Islamic times, until this verse was revealed: Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God.”"
"3845","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, he said: “I asked Aisha, on the authority of God’s saying: There is no sin on him if he circumambulates them. I said: By God, there is no blame on anyone if he does not circumambulate Safa and Marwah. Aisha said: What you said is miserable, O son of my sister. If this verse were as you interpreted it to be, it would be. There is no blame on him not to circumambulate them. But it was revealed that the Ansar, before they embraced Islam, were preparing for the death of the tyrant, which they used to worship at the paralyzed place, and he was one of It was permissible for her to circumambulate Safa and Marwa. When they asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, God revealed that Safa Al-Marwah is one of the rituals of God, so whoever makes the Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame on him for circumambulating them. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, enacted And it is safe to circumambulate with them, so no one has the right to abandon circumambulation with them.”"
"3846","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, who said: “I read about Aisha: There is no sin on him if he Circumambulating them. I said: I don’t care not to circumambulate between them. She said: What an evil thing you said. Some people from the pre-Islamic era did not circumambulate between them. When Islam was established and the Qur’an was revealed, “Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the signs of God, the sign,” the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated, and we circumambulated with him. So it was a sunnah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3847","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Jabir told us, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Safa and said: We will begin with what God has begun. Then he recited: Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of God. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3848","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he left the mosque, intending to row, saying: We begin with what God began with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3849","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Jabir told us, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ascended as-Safa until when he looked at the House he said “Allahu Akbar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3850","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a recitation by him while I was listening, and the pronunciation was his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim. He said: Malik narrated to me. On the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood on Safa, he would say ‘Allahu Akbar’. Three times and he says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things. He does this three times and supplicates. And he does the same on the marwa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3851","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Ja`far ibn Muhammad informed me, that he heard his father He narrates, that he heard Jabir, about the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood on Safa, praising God and praying among \that\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3852","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, circumambulated the Kaaba seven times, abandoned three of them, walked four times, then got up At the Maqam, he prayed two rak'ahs and recited: And they took the Maqam Ibrahim as a place of prayer, and he raised his voice so that the people could hear. Then he went away, so he prayed, then He went and said: We will begin with what God has begun. So he started with As-Safa, and moved on it until the House appeared to him, and he said three times: There is no god but God. Alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. So he glorified God and praised Him, then he supplicated for what was decreed for him, then He descended walking until his feet reached the bottom of the torrent, then he walked until his feet came up, then he walked until he reached the marrow and climbed on it, then he appeared He has the House, and he said: There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. He said that three times, then He mentioned God, glorified Him, and praised Him, then supplicated for whatever God wished, and did this until he finished tawaf.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3853","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi reported, saying: Hatim bin Ismail told us, saying: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, he said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, so I said, “Tell me about the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Jabir said: “We went out with him with no intention other than Hajj. We did not know how to perform Umrah, until we came to the Ka’bah with him. He took the corner, braked for three, and walked for four, then he advanced to the Maqam of Ibrahim and recited the Qur’an. And they made the place of Abraham a place of prayer, and he made the place between him and the House, then he returned to the House and took the corner, then he returned to the door to Al-Safa. When he approached Al-Safa, he said: Indeed, Al-Safa and Al-Marwah are among the symbols of God. Begin with what God began with. So he began with Al-Safa and advanced on it until He saw the House and magnified God alone, and said: There is no god but God, He alone has no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is upon Him. All things are capable, there is no god but Allah, He fulfilled His promise, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone, then He called in between that, and said something like: This was done three times, then he descended to Al-Marwah, until when his feet touched sand in the depths of the valley, until when we ascended he walked until he came Al-Marwah, he did on Al-Marwah what he did on Al-Safa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3854","Imran ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir, He says: “In the Farewell Pilgrimage, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated on his mount around the House and between Safa and Marwah so that the people could see him and ask him that the people \He cheated him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3855","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: al-Thawri reported, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, He said: “I saw Ibn Umar walking between Safa and Marwah, then he said: If I walk, I have seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walking, and if I run, then I have seen I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, running.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3856","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, saying: Sufyan, he is Al-Thawri, told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of many Ibn Juman, he said: “I saw Ibn Umar walking between Safa and Marwah, and he said: If I walk, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walking. And if he runs, then I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, running, and I am an old man.”"
"3857","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Sadaqah bin Yasar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “They asked Ibn Umar, did you see Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sand between Safa and Marwah, and he said: There was a group of people in the sand, and I do not see them sanding except with his sand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3858","Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “It is The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, strove between Safa and Marwah to show the polytheists his strength."
"3859","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Al-Mugheerah bin Hakim, on the authority of Safiyya bint Shaybah, on the authority of a woman, who said “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, running from the depths of the torrent and saying: Do not cross the valley except by hardship.”"
"3860","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down from Safa, he would walk until it came down.” His feet were in the valley, and he strove to get out of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3861","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “When the feet of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were straightened And he descended into the sandy valley until he came out of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3862","Imran ibn Yazid informed me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Ja`far ibn Muhammad informed me, that he heard Muhammad ibn Ali, He heard Jabir talking about the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Then he descended from al-Safa, until his feet were planted in the depths of the valley, and he strove until When we ascended from the other side, he walked.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3863","I am Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi. He said: Yahya bin Saeed told us. He said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us. He said: My father told us. He said: Jabir told us. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, descended, that is, from Safa, until when his feet were planted in the valley, the sand came down until when he ascended, he walked.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3864","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Ismail bin Ja’far reported, saying: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, went to Al-Safa and walked over it until the House appeared to him, then he united and glorified God, and said: There is no god but God alone, with no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things. Then he walked until when his feet were straightened and he ran, until when they ascended. He walked on his feet until he came to Marwah and did on it what he did on Safa until he completed his circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3865","Amr ibn Ali reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr told me that he heard Jabir saying: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah except once.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3866","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Al-Hasan ibn Muslim informed me that Tawus informed him that Ibn Abbas told him on the authority of Muawiyah, “that he shortened the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Mashqas during the Umrah at al-Marwah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3867","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah bin Khalid Al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Muawiyah, said: “I neglected the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Al-Marwah in a desert bed of Bedouins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3868","Muhammad bin Mansour al-Tusi reported, saying: Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Muawiyah, He said: “I took some of the ends of the hair of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a piece of hair that I had with me after he circumambulated the Kaaba and Safa and Marwa in the days of “The ten.” Qais said: And the people deny this to Muawiyah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3869","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: I read to Abu Qara Musa bin Tariq, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Othman bin told me Khathim, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned from Umrah al-Jiranah, he sent Abu Bakr to perform Hajj. So we went with him until he was wearing a garment in the morning, then he sat up to say “Allahu Akbar” and he heard foaming behind his back, so he stood on Takbir, and he said: This is the foam of the camel of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It appeared to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Hajj, so perhaps it That he be the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we pray with him. Then, when Ali was there, Abu Bakr said to him: Amir or a messenger? He said: No. Rather, a messenger. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with a declaration that I would read to the people at the Hajj sites. So we came to Mecca, and when it was before... Al-Tarwiyah: On the day when Abu Bakr stood up and addressed the people, he told them about their rituals, until when he had finished, Ali stood up and recited Bara’a to the people until He sealed it, then we went out with him until the day of Arafat came, Abu Bakr stood up and addressed the people and told them about their rituals, until when he had finished Ali stood up and read to the people a blessing until he sealed it, then the Day of Sacrifice came and we dispersed. When Abu Bakr returned, he addressed the people and told them about And when he had finished, Ali stood up and read to the people a blessing until he sealed it, so when it was the first day of departure Abu Bakr got up and addressed the people. He told them how to march and how to throw, and he taught them their rituals. When he finished, Ali stood up and recited Bara’a on people until he sealed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3870","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported, saying: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, saying: Abdul-Malik bin Abi Sulayman told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jaber, said: “We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the past four days of Dhul-Hijjah, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Permissible.” And make it an umrah. Our chests were filled with that, and it became a sign of pride for us. This reached the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O people, make it permissible. Were it not for the guidance that is with me, I would have done the same as you are doing. We were lawful until we had intercourse with women, and we did what was lawful until the day came. Al-Tarwiyah, and We made Mecca at noon, worthy of Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3871","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr bin Halhalah al-Du’ali, on the authority of Muhammad bin Imran al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, said: “Abdullah bin Omar came back to me, and I was descending under He went on a journey on the road to Mecca, and he said: What brought you down under this tree? I said: Its shade brought me down. Abdullah bin Omar said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “If you are between the two trees in Mina, and he blows his hand towards the east, then there is a valley called Al-Sirba.” The hadith of Al-Harith: It is said, “The Secrets” contains a sermon under which seventy prophets were secreted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3872","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told me, and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told me, they said: Ishaq told us He is Al-Azraq, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi’, who said: “I asked Anas ibn Malik, I said: Tell me about something that you have reasoned about.” On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, where did he pray the noon prayer on the day of al-Tarwiyah? He said: In Mina, I said: where did he pray the afternoon prayer on the day of the Battle? He said: in al-Abtah \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3873","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “We entered on Jabir bin Abdullah, so I said, “Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rode and prayed in Mina? Noon, afternoon, sunset, evening, and morning, then he stayed for a little while until the sun rose.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3874","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, saying: Hammad, who is Ibn Zaid, told us on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: “We went in the morning with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Mina to Arafat, and among us was the one who recited the Talbiyah, and some of us was the one who magnified God.” \""
3875"""
"3875","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi informed us, saying: Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: ""We set out in the morning with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Mina to 'Arafat; among us were those reciting the Talbiyah, and among us were those saying the Takbir."""
"3876","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Malali, whose name is Al-Fadl bin Dukayn, reported, saying: Malik told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told me, he said “I said to Anas, as we were going from Mina to Arafat: What were you doing in reciting the Talbiyah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this regard?” Today? He said: The one who was praying was reciting the Talbiyah, so he was not denounced, and the one who said “Allahu Akbar” was reciting the Talbiyah, but he was not denounced.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3877","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Rajaa told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, he said: “I told Anas The morning after Arafah: What do you say in the Talbiyah on this day? He said: I walked this path with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions, and that was it. “Among them is the forbearer, and among them is the magnifier, so do not deny any of them to its owner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3878","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Kufi al-Awdi reported, on the authority of Khalid ibn Mukhlid, who said: Ali ibn Saleh told us, on the authority of Maysara ibn Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, said: “We were with Ibn Abbas at Arafat, and he said: Why do I not hear the people reciting the Talbiyah?” So I said: They feared Muawiyah, so Ibn Abbas came out of his tent and said: At your service, O God, at your command, for they have abandoned the Sunnah out of hatred for Ali. \""
3879"""
"3879","Ibrahim ibn Harun informed me, saying: Hatim narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, who said: ""We entered upon Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, and I said to him: 'Inform me about the Hajj of the Prophet (ﷺ).' He said: 'He ordered a tent of hair to be pitched for him at Namirah. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out, and Quraysh had no doubt that he would stand at al-Mash'ar al-Haram, as Quraysh used to do in the Jahiliyyah. But the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed on until he came to 'Arafah and found the tent had been pitched for him at Namirah, so he alighted there.'"""
"3880","Ubayd Allah bin Fadhalah bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abdullah informed us that he is the son of Yazid al-Muqri, he said: Musa told us that he is the son of Ali. He said: I heard my father, narrating, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The day of Arafat and the day of Sacrifice, and the days of sunrise are our festival, the people of Islam, so they are days of eating and drinking.”"
"3881","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Mathrud Al-Masry reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Makhramah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Yunus, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no day on which God frees a servant more than the Fire.” From the day of Arafat, he would approach and brag about them to the angels, and say: What did these people want? Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It is similar to that? Yunus bin Yusuf, from whom Malik narrated"
"3882","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdullah bin Idris reported, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: “He said A Jew to Omar: If this verse had been revealed to us, we would have taken it as a festival. Today have I perfected for you your religion. Omar said: I have learned of the day on which It was revealed on that day, and the night it was revealed was Friday night, while we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat."
"3883","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala reported, he said: Ashhab told me, he said: Malik told me, that Ibn Shihab told him, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah He said: “Abdul-Malik ibn Marwan wrote to Al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf ordering him not to differ from Ibn Umar regarding the matter of Hajj, and when it was the day of Arafat Ibn Omar came to him when the sun had set, and I was with him. He shouted at his pavilion, “Where is this?” Al-Hajjaj came out. He was wearing a musty blanket, and he said to him. He said: What is the matter with you, Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: If you want the Sunnah, he said to him: This is the hour? He said to him: Yes. He said: Pour water on me. Then I would go out to you, and you waited for him until he came out and walked between me and my father, and I said: If you want to follow the Sunnah, then shorten the sermon and hasten. Standing up, he looked at Ibn Umar so that he could hear that from him. When Ibn Umar saw that, he said: He spoke the truth."
"3884","Muhammad ibn Adam al-Masisi told me, on the authority of ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Salamah ibn Nubait, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he will deliver the sermon on the Day of Arafat on a camel. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3885","Amr ibn Ali reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Salamah ibn Nubait, on the authority of his father, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivers the sermon on a red camel at Arafat before prayer.”"
"3886","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told us, on the authority of His father, he said: “We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and I said: Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed.” May God bless him and grant him peace, until he came to Arafat and found that the dome had been made for him with a pin, so he descended with it, until when the sun had set, he ordered the rebellion to be performed. So she traveled for him, until when he reached the bottom of the valley, he addressed the people and said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred to you, just as they are sacred to you today. This is in this month of yours in this country of yours. Indeed, everything related to the pre-Islamic era is placed under my feet, and the blood of the pre-Islamic period is at rest. The first blood shed by our blood was the blood of Iyad bin Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith. He was a nurse among the Banu Sa’d, and Hudhayl killed him, and the usury of the pre-Islamic era. And I will give up usury to Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, for all of it is forfeited. Fear God regarding women, for you have taken them from them. With the trustworthiness of God, and you have made their private parts permissible with the word of God, and that they must not put anyone on your bed whom you hate, if they do that So strike them with a blow that does not hurt you, and you are entitled to provide for them and clothe them with kindness. I have left among you that which you will never go astray after me. You have held fast to the Book of God, and you are responsible for me. So what do you say? They said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the message, performed it, and advised it. He said: With his index finger, he raises it to the sky and lowers it to the earth: “O God, bear witness, O God, bear witness,” three times. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3887","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Musa bin Ziyad bin Hudhaym bin Amr Al-Saadi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying in his sermon on the day of Arafat during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “Know that your blood and your wealth “And your honor is sacred to you, as sacred as this day of yours, and as sacred as this month of yours, and as sacred as this country of yours.”"
"3888","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Malik informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salem ibn Abdullah, “that Abdullah bin Omar came to Al-Hajjaj bin Yusuf on the day of Arafat, when the sun had passed the zenith, and I was with him. He said: Go, if you want the Sunnah. He said: This hour? He said: Yes. Salem said: So I said to Al-Hajjaj: If you want to adhere to the Sunnah, then shorten the sermon and hasten the prayer. Abdul said: Allah Ibn Umar: He spoke the truth.”"
"3889","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, He said: “We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and I said: Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked He made peace until he came to Arafat and settled there. When the sun had risen, he ordered the people to perform the ritual prayer, and it departed for him until, when he reached the bottom of the valley, he gave a speech. Then Bilal called the call to prayer, then he stood and prayed the noon prayer, then he stood and prayed the afternoon prayer, and he did not pray anything between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3890","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray the prayer at its appointed time, except in congregation and at Arafat.”"
"3891","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, on the authority of his father, he said: “We entered On Jabir bin Abdullah, so I said: Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: He rode until the situation came, so he made his stomach He led his camel to the rocks, and he placed the mountain in his hands, and faced the Qiblah, and he did not remain standing until the sun set. The yellowness went away a little when the disk disappeared.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3892","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Hushaym, he said: Abdul Malik told us, he said: Ataa told us, he said: Usama bin Zaid said: “I was the buttocks of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat, so he raised his hands to supplicate, and his camel leaned towards him, and her rein fell off, so he took the rein with one of his hands as he raised it. \his other hand\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3893","Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: “We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, so we asked him about the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he told us that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: All of Arafat is a standing place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3894","I am Qutayba bin Saeed. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, who said: “I led my camel astray.” So I went to seek him at Arafat on the Day of Arafat, and I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing, so I said: What is the matter with this? This is one of the \Al-Hams\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3895","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: Amr bin Abdullah bin Safwan told me, that Yazid bin Shayban, He said: “We were standing at Arafat in a place far away from the parking lot, and Ibn Murabba’ al-Ansari came to us and said: I am the Messenger of God to you. He says to you: Be On your feelings, for you are inheriting from the legacy of your father Abraham.”"
"3896","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Ata, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yamar al-Dili, he said “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat, and one of the people of Najd came to him and asked him about Hajj. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Hajj is Arafat. Whoever joins the night of Arafat before dawn on the night of Friday, his Hajj has been completed."
"3897","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri reported, saying: Sufyan, he is Ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Bukayr bin Ataa, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ya`mar al-Dili, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Hajj Arafat is three days, so whoever He reached Arafat before dawn came, then he had reached Mina. Three days from Mina, so whoever hurries on two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays, there is no sin. \on him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3898","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abu Muawiyah reported, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Quraysh were standing At Muzdalifah, they are called Al-Hums, and all the Arabs stand at Arafat, so God commanded His Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to stand at Arafat, then raise And God revealed: “Then disperse from where the people disperse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3899","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad, known as the harem of Tarsus, told me. He said: My father told us. He said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Usama bin Zaid said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed from Arafat, and I was his companion, and he began to brake his camel until the He spread it out so that it would almost hit the one coming, and he said: “O you who have believed, maintain calm and dignity, for righteousness does not consist in keeping camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3900","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Mahrez bin Al-Wadah, who is a Maruzi sheikh, reported on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Umayyah, On the authority of Abu Ghatafan bin Tarif who told him that he heard Ibn Abbas say: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he hanged his she-camel so that His head touched the middle of his journey as he said to the people: Peace, peace, peace on the eve of Arafat. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3901","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Abdul Rahman, who said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God expanded on May God’s prayers and peace be upon him from Arafat, may he rest in peace, and he commanded us to be calm, then he said: “Perform your rites, perhaps I will not meet you after this year of mine.” And throw something like pebbles.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3902","Abu Dawud reported to Suleiman bin Saif, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed from Arafat, he began to say: Tranquility, servants of God,” he said like this with his hand, and Abu indicated Job with the palm of his hand toward the sky (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3903","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Hisham bin Urwa reported, on the authority of his father, “that he heard Osama, while I was beside him, asked: How did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, walk when he left Arafat? \There is a gap of text"
"3904","I am Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi. He said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, “that he asked On the path of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, he said: He used to walk around the neck, so if he found a gap, he would text and the text would be above the neck. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3905","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi narrated, saying: Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went down to the people that princes visit, and urinated, then he performed a light ablution, and I said: O Messenger God, prayer, and he said: Prayer is before you. When we came to Muzdalifah, the last of the people did not leave until he had prayed.”"
"3906","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, “that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him When he left Arafat, he headed towards the people, and I said to him: Should I pray the Maghrib prayer? He said: Is the prayer in front of you? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3907","Ahmad ibn Sulaiman al-Rahhawi reported, saying: Yazid told us, he is the son of Harun, he said: Yahya reported, that Musa ibn Uqba told him about Kurayb. “He heard Usama bin Zaid mentioning that he was sent with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the eve of Arafat until he returned to the people and decided He needed it, so Osama poured water on him while he was performing ablution, and he said: O Messenger of God, should you pray? He said: The prayer area in front of you?"
"3908","Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Adi bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, On the authority of Abu Ayyub, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Maghrib and the evening prayer at Muzdalifah.”"
"3909","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Maghrib and Isha’ together.”"
"3910","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, prayed the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers at Muzdalifah all together.”"
"3911","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Waki’ told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that “they prayed with one iqama, and said: This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did in this place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3912","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i reported, saying: Abu Nu’aym told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers in congregation, with one iqamah.”"
"3913","Muhammad ibn Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: “I witnessed Sa’id ibn Jubayr He established the prayer in congregation, prayed Maghrib three times, then prayed two rak’ahs of the late prayer. It was narrated that Ibn Umar did that, and Abdullah Ibn Umar narrated, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did something like this in this place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3914","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, that he heard him say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, from Arafat until he, meaning the people, urinated, then performed ablution but did not perform the ablution properly, so I said: Prayer, O Messenger of God. He said: The prayer is before you. So he rode until he came, meaning Muzdalifah. He disembarked and performed ablution and performed it well. Then the prayer was established and he prayed the Maghrib prayer. Then each person brought his camel to rest in his house, then the evening meal was served and he prayed with it, but did not pray anything between them.”"
"3915","I am Amr bin Ali. He said: Yahya told us, he is Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined Maghrib and Isha’ prayers in one iqamah. He did not say the tasbih between them, nor after \One of them\"""""
"3916","Issa bin Ibrahim bin Matrud reported, saying: Abdullah bin Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Umar told him that his father said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered a group between Maghrib and Isha’ with no prostration between them.” He prayed the Maghrib prayer with three rak'ahs and prayed the evening prayer with two rak'ahs.\ Abdullah bin Omar used to perform the same prayer until he joined God."""
"3917","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Durqi reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour reported, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only gave permission to Sawda bint Zum’ah to perform the Ifadah prayer before dawn because she was \a depressed woman\"""""
"3918","Muhammad ibn Adam al-Masisi reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim On the authority of his father, on the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, she said: “I wish I had sought permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as I asked him for permission.” Sawda prayed the dawn prayer in Mina before the people came. Sawda was a heavy and depressed woman, so she asked permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, gave her permission, so she prayed dawn in Mina and performed the prayer before the people came.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3919","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da’eef reported, saying: Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha She said: “Sawda was a large and depressed woman, so she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to go out from the crowd at night, so he gave permission.” To her, Aisha said: I wish I had sought permission from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as Sawda asked him for permission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3920","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: “I am among those who presented The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Muzdalifah during the weakness of its people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3921","I am Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “I was among those who presented the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, on the night of Muzdalifah in the weakness of his family. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3922","Nuh ibn Habib al-Qumsi reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Muammar reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He called for the weak people to leave Muzdalifah at night."
"3923","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif Al-Harrani reported, saying: Abu Asim, Affan, and Suleiman told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mashash, on the authority of Ata’, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered the weak members of Banu Hashim to depart from a crowd at night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3924","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Jabbar reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Salim bin Shawwal, on the authority of Umm Habibah, She said: “We used to babysit during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Muzdalifah to Mina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3925","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ata told us, on the authority of Ibn Shawwal, that Umm Habibah told him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered her to bathe from the congregation to Mina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3926","Muhammad ibn Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, that Mawla To Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, he told him: “I came with Asma’ bint Abi Bakr to Mina with a robbery, so I said to her: We have come to Mina with a robbery.” She said: We used to do this with someone better than you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3927","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, saying: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Kathir bin Mudrik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: “I heard Abdullah performing the talbiyah on the night of Muzdalifah, and he said: Here is the one besides whom there is no god. “I heard the one to whom Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed respond.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3928","Abu Kurayb reported to Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Kufi, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, who is Ibn Umayr, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray a prayer at its appointed time except the Maghrib and Isha’ prayers, both of which they prayed.” in congregation, and he prayed Fajr that day before its appointed time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3929","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, he is Ibn Ayyash, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid say: “Abdullah performed Hajj, so Alqamah ordered me to adhere to him, so I complied with him, so we came to Muzdalifah, and when he When dawn came, he said: Get up. I said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, this is the hour I have never seen you pray in. He said: The Messenger of God prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. Zuhair said: And it was not in the Book of God. He did not pray this hour except this prayer in this place on this day. Abdullah said. They are two prayers that are delayed beyond their appointed time, the Maghrib prayer after the people have reached Muzdalifah, and the morning prayer when dawn breaks. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing that."
"3930","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, he said: I heard Al-Shu’bi, He says: Urwa bin Mudarris bin Abi Aws bin Haritha bin Laam told me, he said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a group, and I said: Did Is there any Hajj for me? He said: Whoever prayed this prayer with us and stood in this position until the end of the prayer, and who performed the prayer before that from Arafat, day or night, has performed it. \His Hajj has been completed and his pilgrimage has been completed.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3931","Ali bin Al-Hussein Al-Durhami reported, saying: Umayyah, he is Ibn Khalid, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sayyar, who is Abu Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, On the authority of Urwah bin Mudarris, he said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have come from my mountain. I did not let There is a mountain on which I can stand. Is there a Hajj for me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who has prayed this prayer with us, and has stood before that? At Arafat, day or night, his Hajj has been completed, and his sacrifice has been completed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3932","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Urwa ibn Mudarris, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever joins a group with the imam and the people when they perform the Hajj has performed Hajj, and whoever does not join the people and the imam has performed Hajj.” But he did not realize it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3933","I am Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail, Dawud bin Abi Hind, and Zakaria, on the authority of Al Shu’abi, On the authority of Urwa bin Mudarris, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing at Muzdalifah, and he said: Who has prayed this prayer with us? Here, then he stayed with us, and he had stopped before that at Arafat, day or night, and his Hajj had been completed.”"
"3934","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he is Al-Qattan, he said: Ismail told us, he is Ibn Abi Khaled, he said: Amer told me, he said: Urwah ibn Mudharis al-Tai told me, he said: “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I came to you from my mountains with a tree that crowned my mount.” I have exhausted myself, and by God, there is not a rope left without me standing on it. Is there a Hajj for me? He said: Whoever prayed the morning prayer is here with us, and he came He had visited Arafat before that, and he had completed his pilgrimage and completed his Hajj.”"
"3935","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Bukayr bin Ata told me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Yamar. Al-Daily, he said: “I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat, and people from Najd came to him, and they commanded a man who asked him about Hajj, and he said: Hajj.” Arafat, whoever comes on the night of Friday prayer before the morning prayer has completed the Hajj of the days of Mina for three days. Whoever hastens on two days, there is no sin on him. And whoever delays, there is no sin on him. Then a man follows it and begins to proclaim it among the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3936","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, so he told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The whole of Muzdalifah is a stopping place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3937","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told us, on the authority of His father, he said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and I said: Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, defended May God bless him and grant him peace, and he hanged the reins for Al-Qaswa, so that her head would hit the back of his saddle, and he said with his right hand: O people, Tranquility, tranquility. Every time he approached one of the mountains, he relaxed it a little while it climbed until he reached Muzdalifah, and he prayed the Maghrib prayer with it. And dinner was given with the adhan and two iqamahs, without praying anything between them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, lay down until dawn came, and he prayed the dawn prayer at that time. The morning light appeared to him, then he rode the crest until he came to Al-Mash'ar, and he came upon him, so he thanked God, united him, glorified him, and praised him, so he did not He remained standing until he reached the top, then he pushed off before the sun rose.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3938","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi reported in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Husayn, who is Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Kathir, who is Ibn Mudarrak, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: Ibn Masoud said, and we are in a group, I heard the one to whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed saying about this. Place: “At your service, O God, at your service”"
"3939","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari reported, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, he said: I heard him say: I saw Omar in a crowd, and he said: “The people of pre-Islamic times did not go out to pray until the sun rose, and they would say: Thabeer has risen. And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disagreed with them, then departed before the sun rose.”"
"3940","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Ashhab, that Dawud bin Abdul-Rahman told them that Amr bin Dinar He told him: Ata’ bin Abi Rabah told them that he heard Ibn Abbas say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with his family.” And the weakness of its people, and we prayed the morning prayer in Mina and stoned the Jamarat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3941","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Abbas, who was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the eve of Arafat and the morning of a gathering To the people when they were driven away: “You must remain calm.” And he was holding his she-camel until, when he entered with a sigh while he was from Mina, he said: “You must take the pebbles with which you throw stones.” Al-Jamarah, and the Messenger of God did not stop saying the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamarat.”"
"3942","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Hisham Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, said: “Usama Ibn Zaid was asked, while I was sitting with him, how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was traveling in Hajj.” Farewell when he paid? He said: His camel was moving along the neck. When he found a gap, he said: (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3943","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i reported, saying: Abu Nu’aym told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God expanded on May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and peace be upon him, and he commanded them to be calm, and he placed the stone in Wadi Muhassir, and commanded them to throw the Jamarat like pebbles. \kidnapping\"""""
"3944","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi, the judge of Basra, reported: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was placed in Wadi Muhassir.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3945","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, he said: We entered upon Jabir. Ibn Abdullah, so I said, “Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, defended, meaning whoever Muzdalifah, before the sun rose. Al-Fadl bin Abbas continued until he came to Wadi Muhassir. He moved a little, then he took the middle road that He took you out at Jamarat al-Kubra until he came to the Jamarat that was by the tree and stoned it with seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble of the removal. He shot from the depths of the valley.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3946","Humayd ibn Masada al-Basri reported on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj and Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman. On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl Ibn Abbas, “He was the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he continued to recite the talbi until he threw \Ember\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3947","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i reported, saying: Abu Nu’aym told us, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, and the pronunciation for it is: Sufyan told us. He is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Habib, who is Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He responded until he stoned the Jamarat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3948","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi reported, saying: Ibn Aliya told us, saying: Awf told us, saying: Ziyad bin Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Al Aliyah, He said: Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me on the morning of Aqaba while he was on his camel: “Bring the gleanings for me,” so I gleaned for him. These are the pebbles of the grave, and when I placed them in his hand, he said: The likes of these, the likes of these, and beware of exaggeration in religion. Indeed, those who destroyed before you were extremism in religion.”"
"3949","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id reported to Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, On the authority of Abu Ma`abad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when they were pushed back on the eve of Arafat and the morning after the gathering: “You must be calm.” And he was holding his she-camel until when he entered Mina, when he descended with a sigh, he said: “You must take the gravel that The Jamarat was thrown at him. He said: And the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gestured with his hand as a man throws his hands. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3950","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Awf, who is Ibn Abi Jamila, he said: Ziyad bin Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the morning of Aqaba while he was standing on his camel: “Bring the cat to me,” and I caught it. He had pebbles, and they were the pebbles of throwing, so he placed them in his hands and began to move them around in his hand. Yahya described moving them in his hand with parables. \These\"""""
"3951","Amr bin Hisham Al-Harrani told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahim, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Husayn Al-Ahmasi, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Husayn, said: “I performed Hajj during the Hajj of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw Bilal holding his fist. His mount, and Usama bin Zayd raised his garment over him to shade him from the heat while he was in Ihram, until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba, then he addressed the people So he praised and praised God, and mentioned many words.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3952","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Ayman bin Nabul told us, on the authority of Qudama bin Abdullah, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba on the Day of Sacrifice on a red-haired she-camel of his own. He was not beaten, nor was he expelled, nor to you, to you."
"3953","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr told me, that he heard Jabir, He says: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stone the Jamarat while he was riding his camel, and he was saying: O people, perform your rituals. I do not know whether I will not perform Hajj after my year.”"
"3954","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat on the Day of Sacrifice as a sacrifice, but after the Day of Sacrifice when the sun had passed the zenith.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3955","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is a revolutionary, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “We sent the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the slaves of Banu Abd al-Muttalib wearing red smearing on our thighs.” And he says: “Abini, do not stone Jamarat al-Aqaba until the sun rises.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3956","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi reported, saying: Bishr bin Al-Sari told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “ “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought his family and ordered them not to stone the Jamarat until the sun rises.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3957","Amr bin Ali told Abu Hafs, he said: Abd al-Ala bin Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah said: Aisha bint Talha told me, on the authority of her maternal aunt Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he commanded one of his wives to leave the crowd on the night of Friday prayer before Jamarat al-Aqabah, so she could stone her stones and stay in her house in the morning.” And Ata’ was He did it until he died"
"3958","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Yazid told us, he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the days of Mina, and he would say: There is no harm. Then a man asked him, and he said: I shaved before I slaughtered,” he said. There is no harm. The man said: I threw stones after the evening. He said: There is no harm. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3959","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Badah bin Adiy, on the authority of his father, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the shepherds to shoot one day and leave another day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3960","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, saying: Malik told us, saying: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abi Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adiy, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the shepherds of the household to throw stones on the Day of Sacrifice.” And the two days after that, they will combine it into one of them.”"
